<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nearer, My God, to Thee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Nearer, My God, to Thee&quot; is a Christian hymn written in 1841 by the English poet and Unitarian hymn writer Sarah Flower Adams at her home, &quot;Sunnybank&quot;, in Loughton, Essex. It retells the story of Jacob's dream in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-genesis">Book of Genesis</a> (28:11–12), in which Jacob, sleeping with a stone for a pillow, sees a ladder reaching from earth to heaven with the angels of God going up and down on it.</p></div>
